<description>
Expand the lower color grid by replacing each pixel with its matching top stencil.

Input structure
The input has a top legend and a lower dense color grid, separated by blank rows.
The legend contains left-to-right 2x2 color swatches and, to their right,
the same number of square neutral-color stencil masks.

Rule
Pair the swatches and stencil masks by left-to-right order. For every pixel in
the lower color grid, paste the paired stencil mask as one output block,
recoloring the mask pixels with that pixel's color and leaving mask holes as bg.

Key insight
The lower grid is not copied directly; it is an index grid whose colors select
the stencil shape from the legend, so each input pixel becomes one square block.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "legend stencil s paired with color swatch s.color",
  "dst": "output block d for a lower-grid pixel",
  "match_cond": "s.color == d.input_pixel_color",
  "transform": "recolor s.mask with d.input_pixel_color; stencil holes remain background",
  "grid_shape": "lower grid height and width multiplied by stencil size"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  background: 0
  grid: 15 rows; width = N*(3+stencil_size+1)-1 cols (determined by legend)
  legend:
    position: top of grid, rows 0..(stencil_size-1)
    swatches: N solid 2x2 blocks of distinct non-bg, non-neutral colors at rows 0-1, starting col 0, separated by 1 bg col
    neutral_color: 5 [observed]; exactly 1 color in legend not in pattern
    stencils: N square stencil_size x stencil_size masks of neutral+bg, left-to-right after swatches (1 bg col gap between groups)
    stencil_constraints: all mutually distinct; top row fully neutral; fill 60-89% neutral; each connected (mostly 1 component)
  pattern_grid:
    position: below legend, separated by 1-3 bg rows; fully dense (no bg cells)
    shape: P x P square, P in 4-7
    colors: exactly the N swatch colors; every color appears at least once
  params:
    N: 2-4 distinct pattern colors
    stencil_size: 3-6 (= legend height)
    constraint: P * stencil_size <= 30 (ARC output limit)
  output: P*stencil_size x P*stencil_size; each pattern cell expanded to its paired stencil recolored with that cell's color; bg where stencil has bg holes

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (no inversion needed; output is deterministic from input)
  steps:
    1. Pick N in 2-4, stencil_size S in 3-6, pattern side P in 4-7 such that P*S <= 30
    2. Choose N distinct non-zero, non-5 colors for swatches; choose ordering
    3. Generate N distinct S x S stencil masks (neutral=5, holes=0); ensure top row all-neutral, fill 60-90%, connected, all mutually distinct
    4. Build legend row-band (height S): place N 2x2 swatch blocks at rows 0-1 cols 0,3,6,...; place N stencil blocks starting after swatches with 1-col bg gaps
    5. Generate a P x P pattern grid using only the N swatch colors, no bg, each color used at least once
    6. Place legend at row 0; leave 1-3 bg rows gap; place pattern grid at arbitrary column offset within grid width
    7. Pad grid to 15 rows total (all bg below pattern)
```
